    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0fe7be63_a6b179a7",
        "filename": "virtualizationservice/vmnic/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 135,
      "author": {
        "id": 1950816
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-10T07:37:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve read `CStr::from_ptr`, but I don\u0027t think so. We cannot ensure `ifr_name` is null-terminated. Right after `ifr_name`, there\u0027s an union type. In case of the string size is equal to IFNAMSIZ and first byte of union value is not zero, `CStr::from_ptr` will violate the buffer.\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/rust/crates/libc/src/unix/linux_like/android/mod.rs;l\u003d629-632\n\nPerhaps it\u0027s null-terminated, but I want to simplify when it\u0027s ensured.",
      "parentUuid": "f793a69a_74822f16",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 133,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 135,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "debba20e88ea4868f5988424330fd3d0cf9cdec0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
